# Testing

Every compiler pass and VM feature change ships with tests. Arrange–Act–Assert; one behavior per test; `unwrap` is fine inside `#[cfg(test)]`.

## Where tests go

| Kind | Location |
|---|---|
| Unit tests | `#[cfg(test)]` module next to the code under test |
| Embedded Phoenix sources | `tests/phx-programs/` — `const` program definitions (smoke, negative, modules, projects, diagnostics) |
| Integration helpers | `tests/phx-test/` — materialize embedded programs to temp dirs, compile/run pipelines, CLI subprocess helpers |
| End-to-end programs | `tests/integration/tests/*.rs` driving full compile/run of embedded programs |
| Examples (demos, not CI fixtures) | `examples/` |

## Materialization

- **Single-file** and **module trees**: per-test `TempWorkspace` under the system temp dir (logical paths under `tests/cli/fixtures/...`).
- **Projects** (including path deps): shared process sandbox in `phx-test::sandbox` so sibling deps like `../math_lib` resolve.

## What to cover, per stage

- **Lexer**: table-driven (`input`, `expected`, `name` per row); one row per token type and edge case (empty input, max length, unterminated literals).
- **Parser**: valid programs assert AST shape; invalid programs assert **error recovery** — the rest of the file still parses and later diagnostics still surface.
- **Typeck**: the core Phoenix guarantees — use-after-move (diagnostic cites the move site), no implicit numeric conversions, branch type unification, Copyable eligibility.
- **Bytecode/verifier**: round-trip encode/decode; malformed modules (bad magic, OOB sections, bad jumps, stack underflow) produce clean errors, never panics.
- **VM**: observable program behavior via integration tests, plus error paths (traps, invalid entry).

Test error paths and edge cases, not just happy paths. When a bug is fixed, add the regression test in the same commit.

Run `just test` for the full workspace. `just test-lang` runs the integration subset when you want a faster language-only pass (parallel by default).

Diagnostic goldens live in `phx-programs` as embedded `expected` strings; regenerate with:

```bash
UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p phx-integration-tests --test diagnostics
```

## `phx-programs` generator (`tests/phx-programs/generate.py`)

Embedded programs in `tests/phx-programs/src/` can be regenerated from on-disk fixtures. **Keep the generator and committed Rust in sync** — future runs of the script must not wipe or drift from hand-edited cases.

### What it reads and writes

| Input | Generated module |
|---|---|
| `tests/cli/fixtures/*.phx` (smoke list in script) | `src/smoke.rs`, `src/single.rs` |
| `tests/cli/fixtures/*.phx` (negative list) | `src/negative.rs` |
| `tests/cli/fixtures/modules/` | `src/modules.rs` |
| `tests/cli/fixtures/*/phoenix.toml` (each project dir) | `src/projects.rs` |
| `tests/integration/diagnostics/{case}.phx` + `{case}.stderr` | `src/diagnostics.rs` |

Run from repo root:

```bash
python3 tests/phx-programs/generate.py
```

Then `cargo test -p phx-integration-tests --test diagnostics` (or `just test`) to verify.

### When adding or changing fixtures

**Pick one workflow and finish both sides:**

1. **On-disk first (preferred for new goldens)** — add `.phx` / `.stderr` under `tests/integration/diagnostics/` or fixtures under `tests/cli/fixtures/`, **add a row to the matching list in `generate.py`**, run the script, commit **both** the on-disk files and the regenerated `src/*.rs`.
2. **Embedded first (ok for small edits)** — edit `tests/phx-programs/src/*.rs` directly **and** update the corresponding entry in `generate.py` (`SMOKE`, `NEGATIVE`, `gen_diagnostics()` `cases`, or ensure on-disk source exists so a later regen does not delete the case).

**Do not:**

- Edit only `diagnostics.rs` / `projects.rs` without updating `generate.py` — the next regen will drop the case or revert goldens.
- Edit only `generate.py` without on-disk `.stderr` / fixture files when the generator reads those paths — regen will embed empty or stale `expected` strings.
- Run `generate.py` when `tests/cli/fixtures/` is incomplete (smoke/single lists reference files that must exist on disk) — the script will fail partway and can leave `src/*.rs` half-written.

### Diagnostic golden cases (`gen_diagnostics`)

Each row in `gen_diagnostics()` → `cases` is `(case_name, kind, file_or_tree, project, entry)`:

| `kind` | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `SingleFile` | Embedded single from `tests/cli/fixtures/{name}.phx` |
| `DiagFile` | Source from `tests/integration/diagnostics/{name}.phx`; golden from `{name}.stderr` |
| `CompileSource` | Inline `.phx` in `tests/integration/diagnostics/{case_name}.phx` |
| `ModuleTree` | Module tree name under `tests/cli/fixtures/modules/` |
| `Project` | Project dir name under `tests/cli/fixtures/` + entry path |

Golden `.stderr` text must match normalized CLI output (path prefixes, gutter `|` alignment). Capture with `phx check`, or use `UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p phx-integration-tests --test diagnostics` and copy the printed block into the `.stderr` file before regen.

### Checklist before committing test changes

- [ ] On-disk fixture + embedded Rust + `generate.py` case list all updated together
- [ ] `python3 tests/phx-programs/generate.py` succeeds (when fixtures tree is complete)
- [ ] `cargo test -p phx-integration-tests --test diagnostics` passes for new/changed goldens
